  "title": "Irregular Verbs – Quick Guide",
  "data": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Irregular Verb Patterns",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Some Hungarian verbs are irregular, meaning their conjugation endings differ from regular patterns.",
          "Instead of memorizing each verb separately, focus on how their endings change for each person."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Example Conjugation Endings (Present Tense)",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Take the verb stem and add the irregular endings according to the person."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tesz-type Verb Example (tesz – does/makes)",
        "list": [
          "Én teszek – I do/make",
          "Te teszel – You do/make",
          "Ő tesz – He/She does/makes",
          "Mi teszünk – We do/make",
          "Ti tesztek – You all do/make",
          "Ők tesznek – They do/make"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Játszik-type Verb Example (játszik – plays)",
        "list": [
          "Én játszom – I play",
          "Te játszol – You play",
          "Ő játszik – He/She plays",
          "Mi játszunk – We play",
          "Ti játszotok – You all play",
          "Ők játszanak – They play"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
